<p>Slovak Prime Minister Robert Fico said on Saturday that the European Union should end sanctions on Russian oil and gas imports, restore flows through the Druzhba pipeline, and reopen dialogue with Moscow, arguing that those steps would help ease an energy squeeze that has deepened during the war involving Iran. He made the comments after a call with Hungarian Prime Minister Viktor Orban, another EU leader who has pushed for a softer line on Russian energy. His remarks come as energy costs climb across Europe. Dawn, citing the International Energy Agency, said the conflict linked to Iran has delayed Gulf shipments and created what the agency called the biggest oil supply disruption in history. The broader backdrop is the EU’s sharp pullback from Russian oil since Russia’s 2022 full-scale invasion of Ukraine, with Hungary and Slovakia described as the only two EU countries still importing Russian oil as of late January 2026.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/2oAMdP7Y3dJeUXl3OcwRZsT8FtOdwYarGNC0HJ8VoRyWpAjqRcsD7lpEM9jUga014rzyvgRZ8ViZT3L3nvVOY-n72tng7VysYZXUjnagDs2j' alt='European Union flags flutter outside the EU Commission headquarters in Brussels, Belgium in this file photo.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Price shock: RT cited European Energy Commissioner Dan Jorgensen as saying oil prices had risen 60% and gas prices 70% in the EU since late February.</li><li>War linkage: Fico said ending the war in Ukraine should be part of the response to the broader energy crisis, alongside any move to restore Russian supply options.</li></ul><blockquote>I am not calling for anything else – only for a return to common sense. The whole EU, and especially the European Commission, are beginning to look like a suicide ship when it comes to energy security - Robert Fico</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Robert Fico: Fico cast the crisis as a policy failure in Brussels, saying the EU was showing &#x27;ideological blindness and incompetence&#x27; on energy security and that Ukrainian actions were making the problem worse. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/637312-fico-eu-energy-policy-suicide/'>RT</a>)</li><li>Ukraine: Kyiv said it was repairing the damaged pipeline infrastructure as quickly as possible after reporting that a Russian drone strike had hit pipeline equipment in Ukraine. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1988652/eu-urged-to-drop-sanctions-on-import-of-russian-oil-and-gas'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/637312-fico-eu-energy-policy-suicide/'>EU acting like ‘suicide ship’ by keeping Russia sanctions – Slovak leader</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/slovak-pm-says-eu-should-drop-sanctions-russian-oil-and-gas-boost-energy-security'>Slovak PM says EU should drop sanctions on Russian oil and gas to boost energy security</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1988652/eu-urged-to-drop-sanctions-on-import-of-russian-oil-and-gas'>EU urged to drop sanctions on import of Russian oil and gas</a> - dawn.com</li></ul>